{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"gh issue view 48 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,state,body,labels,comments,url && printf '\\\\n--- issue 47 detail ---\\\\n' && gh issue view 47 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,state,body,labels,comments,url && printf '\\\\n--- plan F ---\\\\n' && rg -n -C 12 'sub-issue F|M1-F|golden|evaluation' docs/stem-separation-plan.md && printf '\\\\n--- candidate files ---\\\\n' && rg --files -g '*.wav' -g '*.mp3' -g '*.flac' -g '*.aiff' -g '*.RPP' -g '*.vgt' . | sed -n '1,200p'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"Listening evaluation of the real LALAL output. See **[docs/stem-separation-plan.md](../blob/main/docs/stem-separation-plan.md)** — sub-issue **F**.\\n\\n**Depends on #45 (real stems) and #47 (imported in REAPER).** Do not start until both are closed.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- On the golden songs, listen for **interference and damage** in the LALAL guitar and backing stems (residual vocals, warble, lost transients).\\n- Note electric-vs-acoustic, the **effective splitter** (`auto` selection), and `extraction_level` (`deep_extraction` vs `clear_cut`) quality in a findings doc.\\n- Feeds the deferred M7 golden-song evaluation; the decisive test is whether a stem works for practice, not a numeric metric.\",\"comments\":[],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnfA\",\"name\":\"status:working\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"1d76db\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoHw\",\"name\":\"implementer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"0052cc\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEovA\",\"name\":\"priority:low\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"9be9a8\"}],\"number\":48,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"M1-F: Stem-separation evaluation pass on golden songs\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/48\"}\n\n--- issue 47 detail ---\n{\"body\":\"Import the separated stems as `[vgt]` tracks in the open REAPER project. See **[docs/stem-separation-plan.md](../blob/main/docs/stem-separation-plan.md)** — sub-issue **D**.\\n\\n**Depends on #43 (sidecar contract), #44 (paths/namespace), #45 (stem outputs exist).** Do not start until all three are closed.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- Extend `vgt_initialize.lua`: after the mirror, read `analysis.stems.artifacts` and create six `[vgt]` stem tracks — `[vgt] Vocals`, `[vgt] Instrumental`, `[vgt] Bass`, `[vgt] Drums`, `[vgt] Guitar`, `[vgt] Backing (no guitar)` — **time-based** positioning, offset-shifted, GUIDs tracked in `managed_track_guids`, **idempotent** on re-apply (same discipline as existing `[vgt]` tracks).\\n- Resolve files only through the sidecar-recorded artifact namespace; missing/invalid artifacts are **skipped with a clear warning**.\\n- Insert WAVs as time-based media and **verify in a saved real RPP** that REAPER serializes **project-relative** paths (supplying a local file to the API is not proof of serialization).\\n- Concurrency: honor the `stems.in_progress` lease — the ReaScript refuses to apply while a live separation lease is present (see plan §2 concurrency protocol); it writes only ReaScript-owned fields.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- A saved-project test proves six stem tracks are offset-shifted, time-based, project-relative, `[vgt]`-owned, idempotent on re-apply; user tracks and regions remain untouched.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOTcQqas8AAAABK21nrw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mrkkucharski\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Blocked pending prerequisite #45. Issues #43 and #44 are closed, but #45 is still open (status:ready-for-review); this issue explicitly requires all three dependencies closed before implementation starts.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-20T14:45:45Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/47#issuecomment-5023557551\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnlA\",\"name\":\"status:blocked\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"d93f0b\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoHw\",\"name\":\"implementer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"0052cc\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEo6Q\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"fbca04\"}],\"number\":47,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"M1-D: ReaScript import of stem tracks into the project\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/47\"}\n\n--- plan F ---\n333-  `sections.py` (`section_timeline_path`), `status.py` (artifact-path reporting),\n334-  and the repo's fixture-scoped `.gitignore` (replace the old `*.vgt-*.wav` /\n335-  `*.vgt-sections.txt` patterns with `test/**/vgt/`). The `.vgt` sidecar itself\n336-  does **not** move.\n337-- The schema migration creates `artifact_namespace` once and updates new output\n338-  paths. Existing legacy artifacts may be regenerated or copied only when their\n339-  exact prior vgt-owned path is known. Unknown files are never swept by a glob;\n340-  harmless legacy orphans remain unless an explicit cleanup action identifies\n341-  them. Land this before B and D so both learn only the final layout.\n342-\n343-### F — Evaluation pass (priority:low, S)\n344-\n345:- On the golden songs, listen for interference/damage in the LALAL guitar and\n346-  backing stems; note electric-vs-acoustic, effective splitter, and\n347-  `extraction_level` (`deep_extraction` vs `clear_cut`) quality in a findings\n348:  doc. Feeds the deferred M7 evaluation.\n349-\n350-## 4. Sequencing & risks\n351-\n352-- Order: **A → E → B → C → D → F**. A establishes the operation/cache contract\n353-  with no external dependency; E fixes paths before outputs exist; B is the only\n354-  network-touching piece; C supplies durable stage orchestration; D consumes the\n355-  final sidecar/path contract; F evaluates real output.\n356-- **Secrets**: `LALAL_LICENSE_KEY` is environment-only — documented in the\n357-  README, never in the repo or the sidecar.\n358-- **Cost is deliberately higher, not accidental**: five operations per song is the\n359-  fixed recipe because prep is rare relative to practice and quality wins. The\n360-  guard against waste is not fewer splits but **not repeating** them —\n\n--- candidate files ---\n./test/Reaper Project/Media/Paris Metro Punk.mp3\n./test/Reaper Project/Media/The Seven Rivers (Full March - 3_00).mp3\n./test/Reaper Project/Reaper Project.RPP\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
